@Scottmitch I'm not sure. The headers are sent through the `DATA` frame. I'm not sure if there needs to be a separate `HEADERS` frame. Those packets listed above are the only http2 packets being sent back and forth. Here's a screenshot of Wireshark so you can see what exactly I see.

<img width="1680" alt="screen shot 2017-04-05 at 11 10 29 am" src="https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/212864/24719994/8ec5942e-19f0-11e7-8efe-5ac156ef2776.png">

In my opinion, I think we should revert this commit and investigate in a branch. Since it's an optimization, we don't have to worry about a backwards compatible transition plan or anything like that.

@fsareshwala - Reverting sounds good to me but are you able to provide a reproducer? I would like to understand what scenario causes the issue and hopefully fix the root cause.

I will list out the message sequence below and please provide more details so I can try to replicate the scenario:

packet # | direction of packet | description and questions
--|--|--
63 | server -> client | SETTINGS (can you share the contents)
71 | client -> server | SETTINGS (can you share the contents, what does Magic mean)
73 | client -> server | WINDOW_UPDATE (are you expanding the connection window?)
75 | client -> server | HEADERS+DATA (what is the contents and stream ID, is the stream ended)
77 | client -> server | SETTINGS ACK?
83 | server -> client | SETTINGS ACK?

I started to try to put together a reproducer but since I'm not quite sure of the message sequence I think there are pieces missing. Here is what I have so far ... feel free to adjust it to replicate your scenario:

```java
public class TlsPauseTest {
    final int serverExpectedDataFrames = 1;
    final int maxClientStreamId = 3 + (2 * (serverExpectedDataFrames - 1)); // 1 data frame per stream
    final int clientDataPayloadSize = 600;

    @Test
    public void testTlsPause() throws InterruptedException {
        EventLoopGroup group = new NioEventLoopGroup();
        Channel serverChannel = null;
        Channel clientChannel = null;
        try {
            final CountDownLatch dataLatch = new CountDownLatch(serverExpectedDataFrames);
            ServerBootstrap sb = new ServerBootstrap();
            sb.group(group);
            sb.channel(NioServerSocketChannel.class);
            sb.childHandler(new ChannelInitializer<Channel>() {
                @Override
                protected void initChannel(Channel ch) throws Exception {
                    SelfSignedCertificate cert = new SelfSignedCertificate();
                    ch.pipeline().addLast(SslContextBuilder.forServer(cert.certificate(), cert.privateKey())
                            .build()
                            .newHandler(ch.alloc()));
                    Http2ConnectionHandlerBuilder builder = new Http2ConnectionHandlerBuilder();
                    builder.server(true);
                    builder.frameListener(new Http2FrameAdapter() {
                        @Override
                        public int onDataRead(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, int streamId, ByteBuf data, int padding,
                                              boolean endOfStream) throws Http2Exception {
                            dataLatch.countDown();
                            return data.readableBytes() + padding;
                        }
                    });
                    builder.frameLogger(new Http2FrameLogger(LogLevel.INFO, "server"));
                    ch.pipeline().addLast(builder.build());
                }
            });
            serverChannel = sb.bind(new InetSocketAddress(0)).syncUninterruptibly().channel();

            Bootstrap bs = new Bootstrap();
            bs.group(group);
            bs.channel(NioSocketChannel.class);
            bs.handler(new ChannelInitializer<Channel>() {
                @Override
                protected void initChannel(Channel ch) throws Exception {
                    ch.pipeline().addLast(SslContextBuilder.forClient()
                            .trustManager(InsecureTrustManagerFactory.INSTANCE)
                            .build()
                            .newHandler(ch.alloc()));
                    Http2ConnectionHandlerBuilder builder = new Http2ConnectionHandlerBuilder();
                    builder.server(false);
                    builder.frameListener(new Http2FrameAdapter() {
                        @Override
                        public void onSettingsRead(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Http2Settings settings)
                                throws Http2Exception {
                            Http2ConnectionHandler handler = ctx.pipeline().get(Http2ConnectionHandler.class);
                            writeHeadersAndData(ctx, handler, 3);
                        }
                    });
//                    builder.frameLogger(new Http2FrameLogger(LogLevel.INFO, "client"));
                    ch.pipeline().addLast(builder.build());
                    ch.pipeline().addLast(new ChannelInboundHandlerAdapter() {
                        @Override
                        public void userEventTriggered(final ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Object evt) throws Exception {
                            if (evt instanceof Http2ConnectionPrefaceWrittenEvent) {
                                // Send a WINDOW_UPDATE, but execute the job on the event loop to be sure we send after
                                // the SETTINGS frame has been sent.
                                ctx.channel().eventLoop().execute(new Runnable() {
                                    @Override
                                    public void run() {
                                        Http2ConnectionHandler handler =
                                                ctx.pipeline().get(Http2ConnectionHandler.class);
                                        Http2Connection connection = handler.connection();
                                        try {
                                            connection.local().flowController()
                                                    .incrementWindowSize(connection.stream(0), 10000000);
                                        } catch (Http2Exception e) {
                                            e.printStackTrace();
                                        }
                                    }
                                });
                            }
                        }
                    });
                }
            });
            bs.connect(serverChannel.localAddress()).syncUninterruptibly().channel();
            dataLatch.await();
        } finally {
            if (clientChannel != null) {
                clientChannel.close().syncUninterruptibly();
            }
            if (serverChannel != null) {
                serverChannel.close().syncUninterruptibly();
            }
            group.shutdownGracefully();
        }
    }

    private void writeHeadersAndData(final ChannelHandlerContext ctx,
                                     final Http2ConnectionHandler handler,
                                     final int streamId) {
        handler.encoder().writeHeaders(ctx, streamId,
                new DefaultHttp2Headers().method(HttpMethod.POST.asciiName()).path("/" + streamId),
                0, false, ctx.newPromise());
        handler.encoder().writeData(ctx, streamId,
                ctx.alloc().buffer(clientDataPayloadSize).writeZero(clientDataPayloadSize), 0, true, ctx.newPromise())
                    .addListener(new ChannelFutureListener() {
                    @Override
                    public void operationComplete(ChannelFuture future) throws Exception {
                        if (streamId < maxClientStreamId) {
                            writeHeadersAndData(ctx, handler, streamId + 2);
                        }
                    }
                });
        ctx.channel().flush();
    }
}
